manifest.xml + manifest/*.xml: stock /vendor/etc/vintf manifest and HAL
fragments, merged into /vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml by the build.

Changes from stock (merging into one file turns cross-file overlaps into
conflicts, which makes servicemanager reject the whole device manifest):
  - boot @1.0 entry removed (the @1.2 fragment covers it)
  - duplicate MediaTek bluetooth.audio (AIDL) and engineermode entries removed
  - stock lazy CAS service dropped; AOSP's android.hardware.cas@1.2-service
    (base_vendor.mk) installs its own fragment
Validate with tools/check-vintf.sh after `m installclean` (stale fragments in
out/ hide missing entries).

Face unlock (TCL vendor APEX com.tcl.hardware.faceunlock) is disabled: its
service needs libbase.so, which a vendor APEX cannot reach without VNDK.
The declaration (tct-face.xml) is parked in configs/disabled/ so the framework
does not poll for the HAL every second.
